WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:02.201
(Upbeat music)

00:00:02.201 --> 00:00:04.418
- I wouldn't say it's
a bike for lazy people,

00:00:04.418 --> 00:00:05.713
which a lot of people think,

00:00:05.713 --> 00:00:07.976
when they think electric cycles.

00:00:07.976 --> 00:00:10.701
So it's more like, an action bike.

00:00:10.701 --> 00:00:13.284
(upbeat music)

00:00:16.308 --> 00:00:19.891
(Adventurous Upbeat music)

00:00:30.133 --> 00:00:34.202
( High intensity rock music)

00:00:34.202 --> 00:00:38.483
- [Ali] Something between a
motorcycle and a normal cycle.

00:00:38.483 --> 00:00:40.660
- You can control the electric power,

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:43.826
so you choose how much you wanna use it,

00:00:43.826 --> 00:00:46.840
but the actual trial is
really, really tiring.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:49.249
It gives you a good workout.

00:00:49.249 --> 00:00:51.235
- It was just a hobby, really,
at the time it was an idea,

00:00:51.235 --> 00:00:53.287
a concept, you know, let
me build my own bike.

00:00:53.287 --> 00:00:55.639
And, I think it was
about three months later,

00:00:55.639 --> 00:00:58.614
I did have my own bike. It
was my own mountain bike--

00:00:58.614 --> 00:00:59.757
- [Saqud] Frankenstein.

00:00:59.757 --> 00:01:02.259
- Yes, definitely looked
like a Frankenstein bike

00:01:02.259 --> 00:01:04.518
and you had batteries
everywhere, wires everywhere,

00:01:04.518 --> 00:01:07.633
it was faster but it was
just too scary to ride.

00:01:07.633 --> 00:01:08.926
Because it was just too light.

00:01:08.926 --> 00:01:10.658
(upbeat music)

00:01:10.658 --> 00:01:13.486
We thought, “Okay, well at
least the concept was there.”

00:01:13.486 --> 00:01:14.581
- [Saqud] And then we're like,

00:01:14.581 --> 00:01:15.619
“This could be a viable business and,

00:01:15.619 --> 00:01:19.373
“you know, electric bike was something
that was growing in the,

00:01:19.373 --> 00:01:21.435
“around the world.”

00:01:21.435 --> 00:01:23.375
- We have to design a
bike which was more for

00:01:23.375 --> 00:01:25.999
the U.A.E. market, which is
something you can take out

00:01:25.999 --> 00:01:28.217
and actually use on the dunes.

00:01:28.217 --> 00:01:30.803
- Saluki, is a local dog breed,

00:01:30.803 --> 00:01:35.330
which is very skinny, it's
very fast and it's quiet.

00:01:35.330 --> 00:01:39.093
It's a desert dog so it
really fits within our brand

00:01:39.093 --> 00:01:41.426
and that's why we picked it.

00:01:42.644 --> 00:01:45.810
- The fat bikes are made
for the desert, mainly,

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:50.032
and they can go up to 45
km per hour in the desert,

00:01:50.032 --> 00:01:53.487
quietly, without disturbing any wildlife,

00:01:53.487 --> 00:01:56.520
without creating any issues in the desert.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:59.105
And it's a really seamless drive.

00:01:59.105 --> 00:02:00.624
- [Fahad] I mean, that was
one of the amazing things,

00:02:00.624 --> 00:02:03.163
when riding on the bike. The first time,

00:02:03.163 --> 00:02:05.801
you know, desert foxes, I saw desert rabbits,

00:02:05.801 --> 00:02:09.292
I saw bugs, I saw lizards,
things I never saw riding

00:02:09.292 --> 00:02:11.231
my quad around in the back
of the desert, before.

00:02:11.231 --> 00:02:15.142
And it's just, in silence,
it's you and the wind.

00:02:15.142 --> 00:02:17.416
It was phenomenal, just
riding on the ridges

00:02:17.416 --> 00:02:19.919
of the sand dunes. And
then, the sun goes down,

00:02:19.919 --> 00:02:21.717
it's just amazing.

00:02:21.717 --> 00:02:22.814
- [Ali] You've gotta try it. I mean,

00:02:22.814 --> 00:02:25.429
one thing that we've
noticed, anyone that gets on

00:02:25.429 --> 00:02:28.988
these bikes, they come
back with a big smile.

00:02:28.988 --> 00:02:31.738
(Dramatic music)

